The first universal false mutation parsed successfully but hit an unrelated Haskell-backend missing-float-hook path during symbolic search, so I am not counting it as non-vacuity evidence. Per the audit rule, I’m replacing it with a ground false result claim at the explicit satisfying input `["", ""]`; that should isolate the expected “Yes versus Wrong” obligation and avoid treating an infrastructure/backend detour as evidence.
